# SABOTAGE: PP-1/PP-3 (Batch 1, ADR-031) — the framework tenant-plane FAIL-CLOSED resolver.
# Neutralizes `Samen.Web.CurrentOrg`'s `param_trust_disarmed?/1` so it always reports the host
# as disarmed — the ARMED-host branch that refuses to resolve an org from a caller-supplied
# `?org=` on a mount that never adopted the `:authn` seam is defeated, and `resolve/3` falls back
# to trusting the query-param identity in EVERY posture. This restores the exact fail-OPEN the
# W4 dogfood live-reproduced (a cookieless `curl ".../crm/contacts?org=<clinic-org>"` resolves a
# tenant actor for the attacker-chosen org -> unmasked cross-tenant PII). The named tenant-authn
# coverage tests (the reproduce-the-attack RED + the enumerating PP-3 guard) MUST fail with it,
# proving they are refutable and load-bearing on the fail-closed branch.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/tenant_authn_coverage_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RED: armed host, cookieless ?org=<other-org> to the unlabeled CRM contacts mount
# MUST_FAIL: resolves NO org for an unauthenticated ?org=
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/current_org.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/current_org.ex
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/current_org.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/current_org.ex
@@ -300,6 +300,6 @@
   def param_trust_disarmed?(mount) do
     case Samen.Web.Operator.otp_app(mount) do
       nil -> true
-      otp_app -> not Samen.Web.TenantGate.armed?(otp_app)
+      _otp_app -> true
     end
   end
 
